  "query_preview": "..\nIssued 236 PM CDT Tue Oct 27 2026\n\nFriday through Tuesday:\n\nHigh pressure lingers through the first half of Friday, while\nwarm advection driven precip tries to move in from the\nsouthwest. The remaining dry air from the high should keep rain\nat bay most of Friday, save for in southwest WI where some may\nwork in during the afternoon.\n\nModel disagreement then takes hold through the remainder of the\nweekend as the ECMWF, GFS, and Canadian all depict different\nsolutions. The ECMWF, generally shows rain remaining south of\nthe border Saturday and Sunday remaining dry. The Canadian shows\nrain over southwest WI Saturday into the first half of Sunday,\nwhile eastern WI remains dry. Finally the GFS is the rainiest,\nwith on and off light to moderate rain through the weekend over\nall of southern WI. Given this disagreement, the NBM paints \nbroad 15 to 30% PoPs over the region through the weekend, with a\nfairly non- descript window of higher rain potential. With \nHalloween approaching and other outdoor events potentially \nhappening this weekend, stay tuned to the forecast for better \nmodel agreement with time.\n\nEarly next week, a larger weather system does look possible,\nthough the timing and evolution of this system remain in\nquestion given continued model disagreement beyond this weekend.\nAltogether, a more active pattern is expected to return.\n\nCMiller",
